Verse 1:
[D]How firm [Em]a foundation, [G]ye saints of the [Bm/F#]Lord,
[Em]Is laid for [D/F#]your faith [F#7]in His [G]excellent word!
[G/B]What more [A7]can [G]He [Em]say [F#dim]than to you [G]He hath [D/A]said,
[G]To you [D/A]who [Em/B]for [C]refuge to [G]Jesus [Em]have [D/F#]fled?

Verse 2:
[D]"Fear not, [Em]I am with [G]thee, O be not [Bm/F#]dismayed,
[Em]for I am [D/F#]thy God [F#7]and will [G]still [C/G]give [G]thee aid;
[G/B]I'll strengthen and [Em]help [F#dim]thee, and cause [G]thee to [D/A]stand
[G]upheld [D/A]by [Em/B]my [C]righteous, omnipotent [D/F#]hand."

Verse 3:
[D]"When through [Em]deep waters [G]I call thee to [Bm/F#]go,
[Em]the rivers [D/F#]of woe [F#7]shall not [G]thee [C/G]overflow;
[G/B]for I [A7]will [G]be [Em]with [F#dim]thee, thy troubles [G]to [D/A]bless,
[G]and sanctify [C]to thee thy [G]deepest [Em]distress."

Verse 4:
[D]"When through [Em]fiery trials [G]thy pathways shall [Bm/F#]lie,
[Em]my grace, all-sufficient, [F#7]shall [G]be [C/G]thy [G]supply;
[G/B]the flame [A7]shall [G]not [Em]hurt [F#dim]thee; I only [G]design
[G]thy dross [D/A]to [Em/B]consume, [C]and thy [G]gold [Em]to refine."

Verse 5:
[D]"The soul [Em]that on Jesus [G]hath leaned for respose,
[Em]I will not, [D/F#]I will [F#7]not depart [C/G]to [G]His foes;
[G/B]That soul, [A7]though [G]all [Em]hell [F#dim]should endeavor [G]to [D/A]shake,
[G]I'll never, [Em/B]no [C]never, no [G]never [Em]forsake!"
